@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# Frame-only retiming of the current complex words is exactly exhausted
+
+**Negative result. There is no κ claim.**
+
+Four frame retimings have been published for the current whole-owner complex words:
+
+- eumemic's PR501 (the same profile is reached by aliromman's PR495 via chafreaky's PR502 transfer) on PR484's gauge80-kernel42 word;
+- the PR495 schedule carried by Dugongue's PR508 onto its coordinated-gauge word;
+- eumemic's PR507 retiming of its partial-own kernel84 word;
+- PR507's body frames as transferred by Dugongue's PR514 onto its 92-pivot word.
+
+Each was found by heuristic search. This package checks that each is **globally optimal** among all
+frame-only retimings that keep the same interface: scalar payloads and order, helper entrances,
+target levels, centre frames and the fixed compensation/kernel prelude. For the PR484 word, the
+result also holds with the prelude released. Any further complex gain therefore has to change the
+word or its interface, not its frames.
+
+## Model
+
+The model is `code/retime_model.py`. It reproduces the climb rule of PR501's `apply_retime.profile`
+and PR484's `audit_gk.py` exactly. `check.py` asserts that the model's profile equals the repository's
+on the unretimed word and on every case.
+
+The rules are:
+
+- Each register keeps a nested chain of GF(2)-subspaces of F₂⁹.
+- Each gate runs at one common frame for all its registers.
+- Each strict increase is a paid child of rank Δ.
+- Targets must equal their level at the cut, and centres must equal their centre frame there.
+- Every register finally climbs to FULL, or to perp(port) for targets.
+
+## Exact optimisation
+
+`code/retime_ilp.py` works as follows.
+
+1. It propagates the feasible window [L_g, U_g] of every gate globally: minimal frames forward from
+   the starts, maximal frames backward from the finals and the cut. Every feasible retiming lies
+   inside these windows, so each gate's candidate set (all subspaces in its window) is complete.
+2. It splits the problem into independent components. Fixed gates cut the register chains, giving
+   38 components with at most about 1,050 gates each.
+3. It solves each component as a 0/1 program in HiGHS. Pair costs along each register chain are
+   linearised with a tight transportation formulation, and nesting is enforced through compatible
+   pairs.
+
+The objective is Σ_children d·(73/d)^b₀, where b₀ is the word's own exact moment root. The moment
+left-hand side is linear in the child counts and increasing in b. A retiming that strictly raises b
+would therefore strictly lower this objective at b₀. The solver finds no such retiming: every
+component reaches the published frames' objective with gap 0.
+
+| case | prelude fixed | b₀ | ILP optimum = published local profile |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| PR501 on PR484 word | 531 (also 0) | 0.001371467217183061 | {1:2385, 2:264, 3:530, 4:84, 5:270, 6:92, 7:1, 8:17} |
+| PR508 collapsed word | 531 (also 0) | 0.001374441333828160 | {1:2385, 2:248, 3:530, 4:88, 5:270, 6:96, 7:1, 8:17} |
+| PR507 partial-own word | 671 (also 0) | 0.001389978441615608 | {1:2493, 2:224, 3:516, 4:84, 5:298, 6:64, 7:1, 8:17} |
+| PR514 92-pivot word (PR507 body frames transferred) | 651 (also 0) | 0.001393462495344162 | {1:2539, 2:160, 3:530, 4:88, 5:298, 6:68, 7:1, 8:17} |
+
+As a control, starting from the unretimed PR484 word (profile {1:2057, 2:928, …}) reaches the PR501
+optimum, so the result does not depend on the published frames. A non-nested frame is rejected.
+
+```sh
+python3 -m pip install numpy scipy   # tested: Python 3.14.6, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1 (HiGHS)
+python3 -B research/exact-retiming-optimality/check.py /absolute/new/output
+```
+
+Single-gate descent, annealing and forward/backward cascade moves from either start also never beat
+PR501. They are weaker than the ILP and are not included.
+
+## Scope
+
+- **Solver tolerance.** This is a floating MILP certificate at gap 0, not an exact rational dual
+  certificate.
+- **Fallback term.** The 10⁻¹⁶ bad-cover fallback term (about 2·10⁻¹³ relative per child) is not in
+  the objective.
+- **Coverage.** Optimality is shown only for frame-only changes under the stated fixed interface.
+  Changing payloads, entrances, gauges, kernel pivots or the factory is outside the claim. It also
+  says nothing about the inherited all-size or analytic contracts.
+
+## Provenance of the words
+
+`CASES.json` gives the hashes and origins of the words.
+
+- **PR484 word.** Rebuilt by the PR505 pipeline. It equals the PR501-pinned source except for three
+  non-proof report floats (`baseline_b`, `complex_coarse_float`, `gain_percent_float`), whose last
+  digits are platform-dependent. With the publisher's values 0.0011839865492062917 and
+  18.471088665044633, PR501's pinned source and candidate hashes are reproduced exactly.
+- **PR508 and PR514 words.** Produced by their own verifiers.
+- **PR507 word.** Built by PR507's verifier up to its unretimed word, then PR507's map was applied with
+  per-entry old-frame checks. PR507's and PR501's published verifiers stop at this hash on
+  Linux/Python 3.14.6 for the float reason above.
+
+## Credits and disclosure
+
+The words and frame maps belong to their authors:
+
+- PR484: DreamingOfClouds, with the earlier PR433/425/442 chain.
+- PR495: aliromman. PR501 and PR507: eumemic. PR502: chafreaky.
+- PR505, PR508 and PR514: Dugongue. PR493: eumemic.
+
+This package adds only the model, the exact solver and the checks. Prepared with Anthropic Claude
+(Claude Code) assistance. Apache-2.0.
